# Simultaneous close: both sides send FIN before receiving peer's FIN
# Client: 10.0.0.1:7000 -> Server: 10.0.0.2:80
# ISN_client=3000, ISN_server=4000
# Client sends 50 bytes, then both sides close concurrently
#
# ts_ms  src               dst               flags seq  ack  win    payload
0        10.0.0.1:7000     10.0.0.2:80       S     3000 0    65535  0
50       10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:7000     SA    4000 3001 32768  0
55       10.0.0.1:7000     10.0.0.2:80       A     3001 4001 65535  0
# Client sends 50 bytes
100      10.0.0.1:7000     10.0.0.2:80       PA    3001 4001 65535  50
150      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:7000     A     4001 3051 32768  0
# Client initiates close
200      10.0.0.1:7000     10.0.0.2:80       FA    3051 4001 65535  0
# Server's FIN crosses in flight (hasn't seen client's FIN yet)
# ack=3051 does NOT acknowledge client's FIN (needs ack=3052)
210      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:7000     FA    4001 3051 32768  0
# Client ACKs server's FIN
260      10.0.0.1:7000     10.0.0.2:80       A     3052 4002 65535  0
# Server ACKs client's FIN
270      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:7000     A     4002 3052 32768  0
